{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":4167,"output":1028,"cacheRead":21920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":172,"totalTokens":27115,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":2,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ed2c21a4-30ce-46b7-bac1-025ed6ee79d7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries (plan + verdict)\nchain = []\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\ne1 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb').write(raw1)\nchain.append((e1, hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()))\n\ne2 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': chain[0][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb').write(raw2)\nchain.append((e2, hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore bundle for entry 2 (range head)\n# We need to stub check_sigstore to return an old attestation time\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 100 * 3600  # 100 hours ago\n\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args):\n    return (old_time, R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2), 'c0ffee')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args):\n    return None  # pending\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ntry:\n    # Test without --max-pending-hours (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\n    print(f'Without --max-pending-hours: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=50 (should fail, 100 > 50)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '50'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=50: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=150 (should pass, 100 < 150)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '150'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=150: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue. The test stubs `check_ots` to return `None` (which means \"pending\"). My new code calls `check_ots` again in the loop that checks for pending proofs. The stub returns `None`, and since `max_pending_hours` is not set (it's `None` by default), the check should be skipped. But wait, my code checks `elif a.max_pending_hours is not None:` before calling `check_ots` again. So if `max_pending_hours` is not provided, the check should be skipped entirely.\n\nLet me verify the test still passes - it did pass in the test run above. Good.\n\nNow, let me also test the new functionality with a manual test to make sure it works as expected. Let me create a simple test scenario.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"I see the issue. The test stubs `check_ots` to return `None` (which means \\\"pending\\\"). My new code calls `check_ots` again in the loop that checks for pending proofs. The stub returns `None`, and since `max_pending_hours` is not set (it's `None` by default), the check should be skipped. But wait, my code checks `elif a.max_pending_hours is not None:` before calling `check_ots` again. So if `max_pending_hours` is not provided, the check should be skipped entirely.\\n\\nLet me verify the test still passes - it did pass in the test run above. Good.\\n\\nNow, let me also test the new functionality with a manual test to make sure it works as expected. Let me create a simple test scenario.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The test passes. Now let me write a quick manual test to verify the new `--max-pending-hours` functionality:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ed2c21a4-30ce-46b7-bac1-025ed6ee79d7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries (plan + verdict)\nchain = []\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\ne1 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb').write(raw1)\nchain.append((e1, hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()))\n\ne2 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': chain[0][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb').write(raw2)\nchain.append((e2, hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore bundle for entry 2 (range head)\n# We need to stub check_sigstore to return an old attestation time\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 100 * 3600  # 100 hours ago\n\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args):\n    return (old_time, R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2), 'c0ffee')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args):\n    return None  # pending\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ntry:\n    # Test without --max-pending-hours (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\n    print(f'Without --max-pending-hours: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=50 (should fail, 100 > 50)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '50'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=50: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=150 (should pass, 100 < 150)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '150'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=150: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":4167,"output":1028,"cacheRead":21920,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":172,"totalTokens":27115,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794917393485,"responseId":"gen-1794917393-35sUWz0xpNK9ka1gIYnS","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":17082,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}}
{"type":"tool_execution_start","toolCallId":"call-ed2c21a4-30ce-46b7-bac1-025ed6ee79d7","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries (plan + verdict)\nchain = []\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\ne1 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb').write(raw1)\nchain.append((e1, hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()))\n\ne2 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': chain[0][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb').write(raw2)\nchain.append((e2, hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore bundle for entry 2 (range head)\n# We need to stub check_sigstore to return an old attestation time\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 100 * 3600  # 100 hours ago\n\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args):\n    return (old_time, R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2), 'c0ffee')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args):\n    return None  # pending\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ntry:\n    # Test without --max-pending-hours (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\n    print(f'Without --max-pending-hours: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=50 (should fail, 100 > 50)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '50'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=50: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=150 (should pass, 100 < 150)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '150'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=150: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call-ed2c21a4-30ce-46b7-bac1-025ed6ee79d7","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries (plan + verdict)\nchain = []\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\ne1 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb').write(raw1)\nchain.append((e1, hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()))\n\ne2 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': chain[0][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb').write(raw2)\nchain.append((e2, hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore bundle for entry 2 (range head)\n# We need to stub check_sigstore to return an old attestation time\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 100 * 3600  # 100 hours ago\n\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args):\n    return (old_time, R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2), 'c0ffee')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args):\n    return None  # pending\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ntry:\n    # Test without --max-pending-hours (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\n    print(f'Without --max-pending-hours: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=50 (should fail, 100 > 50)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '50'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=50: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=150 (should pass, 100 < 150)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '150'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=150: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""},"partialResult":{"content":[]}}
{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call-ed2c21a4-30ce-46b7-bac1-025ed6ee79d7","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create two entries (plan + verdict)\nchain = []\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\ne1 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb').write(raw1)\nchain.append((e1, hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()))\n\ne2 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': chain[0][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb').write(raw2)\nchain.append((e2, hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create a sigstore bundle for entry 2 (range head)\n# We need to stub check_sigstore to return an old attestation time\nold_time = int(time.time()) - 100 * 3600  # 100 hours ago\n\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\ndef stub_check_sigstore(*args):\n    return (old_time, R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2), 'c0ffee')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args):\n    return None  # pending\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ntry:\n    # Test without --max-pending-hours (should pass)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors'])\n    print(f'Without --max-pending-hours: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=50 (should fail, 100 > 50)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '50'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=50: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=150 (should pass, 100 < 150)\n    rc, out, err = R.main(['--ledger', d, 'check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '150'])\n    print(f'With --max-pending-hours=150: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"BAD: entries 1-2 were never attested by the writer\n"}],"details":{}}}
