{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":3461,"output":369,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":19,"totalTokens":34518,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an opt-in `--max-pending-hours H` option to `python3 record/record.py check-anchors`:\n\n### Changes to `/workspace/record/record.py`:\n\n1. **Added `time` import** (line 19)\n\n2. **Added `--max-pending-hours` argument** to the `check-anchors` subparser (lines 626-627)\n\n3. **Modified `cmd_check_anchors` function** to:\n   - Track attestation times for each range head (from sigstore bundles)\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head's OTS proof\n   - If the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is older than H hours, report a `BAD` message with format `\"still pending N h\"` and exit 1\n\n### Behavior:\n- **Without `--max-pending-hours`**: Unchanged - pending proofs are accepted (exit 0)\n- **With `--max-pending-hours H`**: If any range head's OTS proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is more than H hours ago, exit 1 with message containing `still pending N h` (where N is whole hours since attestation)\n- **Pending proof younger than H hours**: Accepted (exit 0)\n- **Confirmed proofs**: Always accepted regardless of attestation age\n\n### Tests:\n- All 21 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` pass\n- Manual testing confirms the new functionality works correctly for single and multiple range heads"}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes made.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes made.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an opt-in `--max-pending-hours H` option to `python3 record/record.py check-anchors`:\n\n### Changes to `/workspace/record/record.py`:\n\n1. **Added `time` import** (line 19)\n\n2. **Added `--max-pending-hours` argument** to the `check-anchors` subparser (lines 626-627)\n\n3. **Modified `cmd_check_anchors` function** to:\n   - Track attestation times for each range head (from sigstore bundles)\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head's OTS proof\n   - If the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is older than H hours, report a `BAD` message with format `\"still pending N h\"` and exit 1\n\n### Behavior:\n- **Without `--max-pending-hours`**: Unchanged - pending proofs are accepted (exit 0)\n- **With `--max-pending-hours H`**: If any range head's OTS proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is more than H hours ago, exit 1 with message containing `still pending N h` (where N is whole hours since attestation)\n- **Pending proof younger than H hours**: Accepted (exit 0)\n- **Confirmed proofs**: Always accepted regardless of attestation age\n\n### Tests:\n- All 21 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` pass\n- Manual testing confirms the new functionality works correctly for single and multiple range heads"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":3461,"output":369,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":19,"totalTokens":34518,"cos