ce/record/test_record.py:30: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedReader name='/tmp/tmpe5gi5gch/entries/000001.json'>\n  return {\"seq\": n, \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(open(self.entry(n), \"rb\").read()).hexdigest()}\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\ntest_wrong_data_exits_1_not_3 (test_record.Ledger.test_wrong_data_exits_1_not_3) ... /workspace/record/test_record.py:173: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedReader name='/tmp/tmp7wbz1ssn/entries/000001.json'>\n  raw = open(self.entry(1), \"rb\").read().replace(b'\"claim\":\"mlp beats linear\"', b'\"claim\":\"\\\\ud800\"')\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\n/workspace/record/test_record.py:174: ResourceWarning: unclosed file <_io.BufferedWriter name='/tmp/tmp7wbz1ssn/entries/000001.json'>\n  open(self.entry(1), \"wb\").write(raw)\nResourceWarning: Enable tracemalloc to get the object allocation traceback\nok\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 21 tests in 0.065s\n\nOK (skipped=1)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":122,"timestamp":1794917515570},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All 21 tests pass (1 skipped). The implementation is complete and working correctly.\n\nLet me also verify the error message format matches the requirement: \"still pending N h\" where N is the whole number of hours. In my test output, it showed \"still pending 100 h\" which matches.\n\nLet me also verify the implementation handles edge cases:\n1. Multiple range heads with pending proofs - should check each\n2. The hours calculation uses integer division (floor) - correct\n3. The message format is \"still pending N h\" - correct\n\nLet me also check if there are any issues with the code when there are multiple range heads.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All 21 tests pass (1 skipped). The implementation is complete and working correctly.\\n\\nLet me also verify the error message format matches the requirement: \\\"still pending N h\\\" where N is the whole number of hours. In my test output, it showed \\\"still pending 100 h\\\" which matches.\\n\\nLet me also verify the implementation handles edge cases:\\n1. Multiple range heads with pending proofs - should check each\\n2. The hours calculation uses integer division (floor) - correct\\n3. The message format is \\\"still pending N h\\\" - correct\\n\\nLet me also check if there are any issues with the code when there are multiple range heads.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Let me also test with multiple range heads to ensure the implementation handles that correctly:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ba3c2b1c-2ff2-4b3b-b2f6-426f042c00a8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport tempfile, os, json, hashlib, time, io, contextlib\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a test ledger with 4 entries (2 ranges)\nd = tempfile.mkdtemp()\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'entries'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'anchors'))\nos.makedirs(os.path.join(d, 'inbox'))\n\n# Create 4 entries\nchain = []\nPLAN = {'by': 'proposer-agent', 'claim': 'mlp beats linear', 'test': 'count.py ...', 'decision_rule': 'Ir lower by > 2 SE'}\n\n# Entry 1: plan\ne1 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000001.json'), 'wb').write(raw1)\nchain.append((e1, hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()))\n\n# Entry 2: verdict for plan 1 (range head 1)\ne2 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': chain[0][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000002.json'), 'wb').write(raw2)\nchain.append((e2, hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()))\n\n# Entry 3: plan 2\ne3 = R.make_entry(chain, 'plan', PLAN, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw3 = R.canonical(e3)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000003.json'), 'wb').write(raw3)\nchain.append((e3, hashlib.sha256(raw3).hexdigest()))\n\n# Entry 4: verdict for plan 2 (range head 2)\ne4 = R.make_entry(chain, 'verdict', {'by': 'verifier-agent', 'plan': {'seq': 3, 'sha256': chain[2][1]}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}, now='2024-01-01T12:00:00Z')\nraw4 = R.canonical(e4)\nopen(os.path.join(d, 'entries', '000004.json'), 'wb').write(raw4)\nchain.append((e4, hashlib.sha256(raw4).hexdigest()))\n\n# Create sigstore and OTS anchor files for both range heads (entries 2 and 4)\nfor seq in [2, 4]:\n    open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', f'{seq:06d}.sigstore.json'), 'w').write('{}')\n    open(os.path.join(d, 'anchors', f'{seq:06d}.ots'), 'wb').write(b'stub')\n\n# Stub check_sigstore to return different attestation times for each range head\n# Entry 2: 100 hours ago (old)\n# Entry 4: 10 hours ago (recent)\ndef stub_check_sigstore(path, entry_digest, repo, workflow, ref):\n    seq = int(os.path.basename(path).split('.')[0])\n    if seq == 2:\n        return (int(time.time()) - 100 * 3600, R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2), 'c0ffee')\n    else:  # seq == 4\n        return (int(time.time()) - 10 * 3600, R.range_predicate(chain, 3, 4), 'deadbeef')\n\ndef stub_check_ots(*args):\n    return None  # both pending\n\noriginal_check_sigstore = R.check_sigstore\noriginal_check_ots = R.check_ots\n\nR.check_sigstore = stub_check_sigstore\nR.check_ots = stub_check_ots\n\ndef run_cmd(*args):\n    out, err = io.StringIO(), io.StringIO()\n    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(out), contextlib.redirect_stderr(err):\n        rc = R.main(['--ledger', d, *args])\n    return rc, out.getvalue(), err.getvalue()\n\ntry:\n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=50 (should fail for entry 2, pass for entry 4)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '50')\n    print(f'--max-pending-hours=50: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\n    \n    # Test with --max-pending-hours=150 (should pass for both)\n    rc, out, err = run_cmd('check-anchors', '--max-pending-hours', '150')\n    print(f'--max-pending-hours=150: rc={rc}')\n    print(f'  stderr: {err.strip()}')\nfinally:\n    R.check_sigstore = original_check_sigstore\n    R.check_ots = original_check_ots\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(d)\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":1580,"output":1413,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":135,"totalTokens":33681,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794917515572,"responseId":"gen-1794917515-5jEkSOH2vWXZCIhMEfIx","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":19832,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-ba3c2b1c-2ff2-4b3b-b2f6-426f042c00a8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"--max-pending-hours=50: rc=1\n  stderr: BAD: anchors/000002.ots: still pending 100 h\n--max-pending-hours=150: rc=0\n  stderr: \n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":50,"timestamp":1794917535454},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The implementation correctly handles multiple range heads - it only flags the one that exceeds the threshold (entry 2 at 100 hours) and not the recent one (entry 4 at 10 hours).\n\nThe implementation is complete and working correctly. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n1. Added `--max-pending-hours` argument to the `check-anchors` subparser\n2. Added `import time` to the imports\n3. Modified `cmd_check_anchors` to:\n   - Track attestation times for each range head (from sigstore)\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head's OTS proof\n   - If the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is older than H hours, add a \"BAD\" message with \"still pending N h\" format\n4. All existing tests pass\n5. Manual tests confirm the new functionality works as expected\n\nThe implementation meets all the requirements:\n- Without the option, behavior is unchanged (pending proofs accepted, exit 0)\n- With the option, if any range head's proof is pending and attestation is > H hours ago, exit 1 with message containing \"still pending N h\"\n- A pending proof younger than H hours is fine (exit 0)\n- All existing tests pass","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The implementation correctly handles multiple range heads - it only flags the one that exceeds the threshold (entry 2 at 100 hours) and not the recent one (entry 4 at 10 hours).\\n\\nThe implementation is complete and working correctly. Let me summarize what was done:\\n\\n1. Added `--max-pending-hours` argument to the `check-anchors` subparser\\n2. Added `import time` to the imports\\n3. Modified `cmd_check_anchors` to:\\n   - Track attestation times for each range head (from sigstore)\\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head's OTS proof\\n   - If the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is older than H hours, add a \\\"BAD\\\" message with \\\"still pending N h\\\" format\\n4. All existing tests pass\\n5. Manual tests confirm the new functionality works as expected\\n\\nThe implementation meets all the requirements:\\n- Without the option, behavior is unchanged (pending proofs accepted, exit 0)\\n- With the option, if any range head's proof is pending and attestation is > H hours ago, exit 1 with message containing \\\"still pending N h\\\"\\n- A pending proof younger than H hours is fine (exit 0)\\n- All existing tests pass\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The implementation correctly handles multiple range heads - only the one exceeding the threshold is flagged. Let me run the tests one final time to confirm everything is working:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-2a83197e-2f47-4786-97a0-d352a5893137","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -m unittest test_record 2>&1 | tail -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":3068,"output":351,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":275,"totalTokens":34107,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794917535456,"responseId":"gen-1794917535-wjo0gN5eFJgFyWQBEGXe","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":8088,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call-2a83197e-2f47-4786-97a0-d352a5893137","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":".\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 21 tests in 0.052s\n\nOK (skipped=1)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":110,"timestamp":1794917543653},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes made.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me provide a summary of the changes made.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. The implementation is complete. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an opt-in `--max-pending-hours H` option to `python3 record/record.py check-anchors`:\n\n### Changes to `/workspace/record/record.py`:\n\n1. **Added `time` import** (line 19)\n\n2. **Added `--max-pending-hours` argument** to the `check-anchors` subparser (lines 626-627)\n\n3. **Modified `cmd_check_anchors` function** to:\n   - Track attestation times for each range head (from sigstore bundles)\n   - When `--max-pending-hours` is provided, check each range head's OTS proof\n   - If the proof is pending (returns `None`) and the attestation time is older than H hours, report a `BAD` message with format `\"still pending N h\"` and exit 1\n\n### Behavior:\n- **Without `--max-pending-hours`**: Unchanged - pending proofs are accepted (exit 0)\n- **With `--max-pending-hours H`**: If any range head's OTS proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is more than H hours ago, exit 1 with message containing `still pending N h` (where N is whole hours since attestation)\n- **Pending proof younger than H hours**: Accepted (exit 0)\n- **Confirmed proofs**: Always accepted regardless of attestation age\n\n### Tests:\n- All 21 existing tests in `record/test_record.py` pass\n- Manual testing confirms the new functionality works correctly for single and multiple range heads"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free","usage":{"input":3461,"output":369,"cacheRead":30688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":19,"totalTokens":34518,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":true}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1794917543655,"responseId":"gen-1794917543-AoFrjMaftVLU55A4SFNF","rawStopReason":"stop","durationMs":8243,"thinkingLevel":"medium"}],"willRetry":false}
